// B2 course (B1 → B2 roadmap), module 8 „Reisimine ja kultuur” (b1b2-036…040), stage B2-.
// Lesson template v4 (docs/COURSE_DESIGN_COMMUNICATIVE.md §12). One storyline, a year after the B1 course: the Kase kool
// family club („pereklubi”, led by Jaan) brings Estonian families and families who moved to Estonia together. Topic added
// to the B2 course here: IDENTITY — who am I between two cultures and languages, belonging, traditions (Sofia, Olena and
// Daria, Ruslan; Setomaa and leelo, jaanipäev, laulupidu). One goal said on the first sheet: at the end the learner gives a
// short talk „Kaks kodu” at the school's culture evening and writes a travel story for the city magazine „Linnaelu”
// (039 Kasuta).
// Grammar (spiral, docs/METHODOLOGY_STANDARD.md §5): kes/mis relative clauses with the pronoun's case (kus, kuhu, kust,
// mille, kellel, kellega — 036, back in 037 and 039); the quotative for reported claims — olevat, ei olevat, olevat olnud,
// tema sõnul, väidetavalt (037, back in 039); the essive of a role or a time — müüjana, uustulnukana, lapsena — against the
// translative of change or opinion — saada tõlgiks, peetakse eestlaseks (038, back in 039); past tenses and assessment
// in a review (039). Module 7's words return (kool, õppimine, õpetaja, hinne, kursus, keeleõpe, huviharidus, huviring,
// uuring, eesmärk, harjumus, tagasiside, motivatsioon, küsitlus, õpilane, ettepanek, lahendus, seisukoht).
// Harno B2 formats trained: 4-option gap texts (036, 037, 039), listening (036, 037, 038 ×2), the long article with
// multiple choice (038), the sentence-bank text (039), a semi-formal letter (037), an argument text of ~180 words (038),
// the 1-minute monologue on a work topic (036, 038, 039) and the debate with pro / contra cards and a decision (036).
//   036 The family club chooses its spring trip: the newsletter with three options (Setomaa, Viljandi, Saaremaa), Jaan's
//       calls to the bus company and the guesthouse; the club meeting with pro / contra cards, the decision and a letter.
//   037 The Setomaa trip goes wrong: voice messages from the broken bus, Sofia's complaint letter, Aino's story retold in
//       the quotative, a call to the bus company; meanwhile Anna in Rome — the call to the booking portal and a complaint.
//   038 Who am I between two cultures: four people's cards, the radio interview with Ruslan and Olena, the Harno article
//       „Kahe kodu inimene”; Olena's first jaanipäev at Viktor's farm — Kupala night and jaaniõhtu, an opinion piece.
//   039 Reviews and travel stories: Anna's Kihnu review, Olena's laulupidu story (sentence bank), Sofia's Setomaa review;
//       the culture evening „Kaks kodu” — the editor's interview, the talk and the story for „Linnaelu”.
// Final shape (docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_B2.md §4.1 row 8, 2026-10-29): 036 PROJ R→W (corner R2b = the newsletter with
// eight 1–3-word answers, R2b introduced in this module; main = W03 letter to the families: the decision, the costs, the
// deadline), 037 KIRJ L→W (corner R3 = Sofia's complaint as a 12-gap 4-option cloze; main = W13 semi-formal complaint to
// Reisikoht), 038 RÄÄK L→S (corner L4 = the radio interview with two guests, 12 true / false statements, L4 introduced
// in this module; main = S17 argument cards on one joint summer party), 039 LUGE R→S (corner R4 = Olena's laulupidu story
// with a sentence bank and one extra; main = S16 talk at the culture evening, recorded at home). Every teaching lesson:
// review naming the previous lesson and a module 4–6 lesson, a pair task in the lesson, a home recording in Kasuta, two
// fluency tasks; S16 in 036 and 039, S17 in 036 and 038.
// Lesson 5 (040) is the module's check (Vahehindamine 2) in Harno B2 form: R1, R2a, R2b, R3, R4, L3, L4, W1, W2a, S1, S2
// tagged, every part timed with B.examPart. The v3 file is in archive/v3/b2/module08.js.
